---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HowToSchema from '../../components/seo/HowToSchema.astro';
import UpdatedBadge from '../../components/content/UpdatedBadge.astro';
import pricingData from '../../data/ai-pricing.json';

const { subscriptionTools, apiPlatforms, usagePresets, currencies } = pricingData;

// One source for the freshness claim: the same field the disclaimer and the table use.
const verifiedOn = new Date(pricingData.lastUpdated + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC',
});
const apiModelCount = apiPlatforms.reduce((n, p) => n + p.models.length, 0);

const faqList = [
  {
    question: 'What is the Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator?',
    answer: 'The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator is a free, privacy-first browser tool that estimates your true monthly spend across AI subscriptions and API platforms. It covers ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI API, DeepSeek, Kimi, and more than 20 models. Select your stack, choose usage presets or enter raw token counts, toggle between personal and business mode, and see your cost breakdown in USD, EUR, or GBP. Everything runs instantly in your browser. No signup, no server, no data collection.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How accurate are these AI cost estimates?',
    answer: 'Estimates are based on publicly published pricing verified in August 2026. Subscription costs are exact because they are fixed monthly fees. API costs depend on actual token counts, which vary by prompt length, context window usage, and retry behavior. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator adds a 15% buffer to all API estimates to account for real-world overage, so most users find the final bill falls within the predicted range.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between subscription and API costs?',
    answer: 'Subscriptions are flat monthly fees charged per user or account. For example, ChatGPT Plus costs $20 per month regardless of how much you use it. API costs are pay-as-you-go based on tokens processed: input tokens carry your prompt and context, while output tokens carry the AI-generated response. API bills scale directly with usage, making them unpredictable for heavy users but very cheap for light automation.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How many tokens does a typical coding session use?',
    answer: 'A typical vibe-coding session with an AI IDE like Cursor or GitHub Copilot uses 3,000 to 8,000 input tokens for code context and prompts, plus 2,000 to 4,000 output tokens for generated code. A deep research task analyzing large documents can consume 50,000 or more input tokens. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator includes preset profiles for common workflows so you do not need to count tokens manually.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Why is Cursor cheaper with BYOK?',
    answer: 'BYOK stands for Bring Your Own Key. When you use Cursor with BYOK, you pay Cursor\'s base subscription fee plus the direct API costs to Anthropic or OpenAI at raw token rates. Cursor\'s managed plans include bundled API credits that come with a markup. For light users, the bundled credits are enough. For heavy users who process millions of tokens per month, BYOK eliminates the markup and can reduce total cost by 30 to 60 percent.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How can I reduce my AI API bill by 50–90%?',
    answer: 'Switch to smaller models for simple tasks: Claude Haiku 4.5 instead of Opus 4.7, or GPT-5.4 Nano instead of GPT-5.4. Enable prompt caching on Claude and OpenAI to reuse context without re-billing. Use batch APIs for non-urgent work to get 50% discounts. Keep prompts concise to reduce input tokens. For high-volume automation, DeepSeek V4 Flash costs $0.14 per million input tokens, making it the cheapest mainstream option. Together, these tactics typically cut API spend by half or more.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the calculator include VAT or sales tax?',
    answer: 'No. All prices shown are pre-tax in USD, EUR, or GBP equivalents. Sales tax and VAT depend on your billing country and are added at checkout by each provider. For example, EU customers typically pay 20% VAT on top of the listed subscription price. Always check your invoice for the final tax-inclusive total.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the cheapest AI model for high-volume tasks in 2026?',
    answer: 'DeepSeek V4 Flash is the cheapest mainstream model at $0.14 per million input tokens and $0.28 per million output tokens. For OpenAI users, GPT-5.4 Nano costs $0.20 per million input tokens and $1.25 per million output tokens, though it has lower capability. Claude Haiku 4.5 is the most affordable Anthropic model at $1 per million input tokens and $5 per million output tokens. For pure cost efficiency on simple automation, DeepSeek V4 Flash offers the best price-to-performance ratio.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How often is the AI pricing data updated?',
    answer: 'Pricing is reviewed and updated every 90 days. The current dataset was last verified on May 18, 2026. AI providers change rates frequently. OpenAI, Anthropic, and DeepSeek have all adjusted pricing within the past six months. Official pricing pages are monitored and the Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator is updated within one week of any announced change. Always verify on the provider\'s official site before signing annual contracts.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I use multiple AI tools at the same time?',
    answer: 'Yes, and most teams do. A typical setup stacks ChatGPT or Claude for general research and writing, Cursor or GitHub Copilot for software development, and OpenAI API or DeepSeek for production automations and backend integrations. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator lets you select any combination of subscriptions, API platforms, and hybrid setups to see your true total stack cost before any free trials expire.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What does "per seat" mean for AI team tools?',
    answer: 'Per seat means the price is charged for each individual user on your team. GitHub Copilot Business costs $19 per seat per month, so a five-person engineering team pays $95 per month. Some tools like ChatGPT Plus are priced per account, not per seat, which means one person can use it but sharing the login violates most terms of service. Business plans always use per-seat billing to enforce proper user licensing.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Are there free tiers for these AI tools?',
    answer: 'Most platforms offer limited free tiers. ChatGPT Free has daily message caps. GitHub Copilot Free gives 2,000 code completions per month. Cursor Hobby is free for light individual use. DeepSeek provides starter API credits for new accounts. The calculator focuses on paid plans because free tiers are typically too restrictive for daily professional use, but they are excellent for testing before committing to a subscription.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Which AI setup gives the best value for developers?',
    answer: 'For solo developers, Cursor Pro at $20 per month plus Claude API via BYOK offers the best balance of IDE integration and raw token pricing. For teams, GitHub Copilot Business at $19 per seat provides the deepest IDE integration across VS Code, JetBrains, and Visual Studio. If you only need occasional code help, ChatGPT Plus at $20 per month is the cheapest entry point. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator lets you model each scenario side by side.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I calculate API tokens for my project?',
    answer: 'One token equals roughly 0.75 words in English. A 500-word email prompt uses about 667 input tokens. A 300-word response uses about 400 output tokens. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator includes presets for common workflows: vibe coding, document summarization, customer support automation, and research agents. Select the preset that matches your use case and the calculator auto-fills realistic token counts based on industry averages.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Why is my Cursor or Claude bill so much higher than the subscription price?',
    answer: 'Subscription sticker prices are just the entry fee. For power users, actual API-equivalent consumption can be 5–20x higher than the base plan. The biggest hidden drivers are context window re-sending (every turn in a conversation resends the full history), cache operations, file reads, and retries on failed outputs. A developer on Claude Code Max calculated their true API-equivalent usage at over $1,400 per month, seven times the $200 sticker price. Cursor Pro users routinely hit daily limits within an hour of agentic coding. The Best Answer Hub AI Cost Calculator factors in a 15% buffer across all API estimates to account for this real-world overage.'
  }
];

const seo = {
  title: 'AI Cost Calculator — Monthly AI Stack Spend (2026)',
  description: 'Free AI cost calculator. Estimate monthly spend for Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot, OpenAI, DeepSeek and Kimi. Subscriptions and API pricing included.',
  url: '/tools/ai-cost-calculator/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: '2026-05-17T00:00:00+00:00',
  dateModified: '2026-08-29T00:00:00+00:00',
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Tools', url: '/tools/' },
    { name: 'AI Cost Calculator', url: '/tools/ai-cost-calculator/' }
  ],
  faq: faqList
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-10 pb-6 md:pt-14 md:pb-8">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-5">
          <UpdatedBadge date={seo.dateModified} suffix={`${subscriptionTools.length + apiPlatforms.length} tools, ${apiModelCount} API models`} />
          <a href="/calculators/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink bg-white border border-bae-border px-3.5 py-2 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary hover:text-bae-primary transition-colors no-underline shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
            ← Calculators
          </a>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-4">
          AI Cost Calculator:<br/>
          <em class="italic text-bae-primary">Estimate your true monthly spend</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-bae-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Most teams underestimate their AI stack cost by 40–60%. Add your subscriptions, API usage, and hybrid tooling to see what Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Kimi and others will actually cost you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Calculator Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="AI cost calculator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <!-- Controls Bar -->
      <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-4 md:p-5 mb-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-start sm:items-center justify-between shadow-bae-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Currency</span>
          <div class="inline-flex bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm overflow-hidden" id="currency-toggle">
            {Object.entries(currencies).map(([code, info]) => (
              <button type="button" data-currency={code} class={`currency-btn px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors ${code === 'USD' ? 'bg-bae-ink text-white' : 'text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink'}`}>
                {code}
              </button>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink">Mode</span>
          <div class="inline-flex bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm overflow-hidden" id="mode-toggle">
            <button type="button" data-mode="personal" class="mode-btn px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium bg-bae-primary text-white transition-colors">Personal</button>
            <button type="button" data-mode="business" class="mode-btn px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink transition-colors">Business</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_380px] gap-6 items-start">
        <!-- Left: Tool Stack -->
        <div class="space-y-4" id="tool-stack">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mb-1">Subscriptions</h2>
          {subscriptionTools.map((tool) => (
            <div class="tool-card bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-sm overflow-hidden" data-tool-id={tool.id} data-tool-type="subscription">
              <label class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 cursor-pointer hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
                <input type="checkbox" class="tool-check w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded border-bae-border text-bae-primary focus:ring-bae-primary" data-tool={tool.id} />
                <div class="flex-1">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm">{tool.name}</span>
                    <span class="text-[11px] font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary">{tool.category}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-0.5">{tool.description}</p>
                </div>
              </label>
              <div class="tool-config hidden px-4 pb-4 pt-0 border-t border-bae-border-light">
                <div class="pt-3 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Plan</label>
                    <select class="tool-tier w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={tool.id}>
                      {tool.tiers.map((tier) => (
                        <option value={tier.id} data-price={tier.monthlyUSD} data-per-seat={tier.perSeat ? 'true' : 'false'}>
                          {tier.name} — ${tier.monthlyUSD}{tier.perSeat ? '/seat' : '/mo'}
                        </option>
                      ))}
                    </select>
                  </div>
                  <div class="tool-seats-wrapper" data-tool={tool.id}>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Seats</label>
                    <input type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="1" class="tool-seats w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={tool.id} />
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}

          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mt-6 mb-1">API Platforms</h2>
          {apiPlatforms.map((platform) => (
            <div class="tool-card bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-sm overflow-hidden" data-tool-id={platform.id} data-tool-type="api">
              <label class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 cursor-pointer hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
                <input type="checkbox" class="tool-check w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded border-bae-border text-bae-primary focus:ring-bae-primary" data-tool={platform.id} />
                <div class="flex-1">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm">{platform.name}</span>
                    <span class="text-[11px] font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-bae-primary-soft text-bae-primary">{platform.category}</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-0.5">{platform.description}</p>
                </div>
              </label>
              <div class="tool-config hidden px-4 pb-4 pt-0 border-t border-bae-border-light">
                <div class="pt-3 space-y-3">
                  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                    <div>
                      <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Model</label>
                      <select class="tool-model w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={platform.id}>
                        {platform.models.map((model) => (
                          <option value={model.id} data-input={model.inputPer1M} data-output={model.outputPer1M}>
                            {model.name} ({model.context})
                          </option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Usage Preset</label>
                      <select class="tool-preset w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={platform.id}>
                        <option value="custom">Custom</option>
                        {usagePresets.map((preset) => (
                          <option value={preset.id} data-daily={preset.dailyRequests} data-input={preset.avgInputTokens} data-output={preset.avgOutputTokens}>
                            {preset.name}
                          </option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                    <div>
                      <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Monthly Input Tokens</label>
                      <input type="number" min="0" value="0" class="tool-input-tokens w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={platform.id} />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Monthly Output Tokens</label>
                      <input type="number" min="0" value="0" class="tool-output-tokens w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" data-tool={platform.id} />
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}

          <!-- Cursor Hybrid Special Case -->
          <div class="tool-card bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-sm overflow-hidden" data-tool-id="cursor-byok" data-tool-type="hybrid">
            <label class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 cursor-pointer hover:bg-bae-bg/50 transition-colors">
              <input type="checkbox" class="tool-check w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded border-bae-border text-bae-primary focus:ring-bae-primary" data-tool="cursor-byok" />
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm">Cursor (BYOK)</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 border border-amber-100">Hybrid</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-0.5">Cursor subscription + your own API key for cheaper raw token rates.</p>
              </div>
            </label>
            <div class="tool-config hidden px-4 pb-4 pt-0 border-t border-bae-border-light">
              <div class="pt-3 space-y-3">
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Cursor Plan</label>
                    <select class="cursor-tier w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                      <option value="cursor-pro" data-price="20">Pro — $20/mo</option>
                      <option value="cursor-pro-plus" data-price="60">Pro+ — $60/mo</option>
                      <option value="cursor-ultra" data-price="200">Ultra — $200/mo</option>
                      <option value="cursor-business" data-price="40">Business — $40/seat</option>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                  <div class="cursor-seats-wrapper">
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Seats</label>
                    <input type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="1" class="cursor-seats w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">API Provider</label>
                    <select class="cursor-api-provider w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                      <option value="claude-api">Claude API</option>
                      <option value="openai-api">OpenAI API</option>
                      <option value="gemini-api">Gemini API</option>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">API Model</label>
                    {/* Every option carries data-provider so the provider switch scales past two
                        vendors. It replaced a boolean `openai-option` class that could only ever
                        express "OpenAI or not". Prices are per 1M tokens, verified against each
                        vendor's own pricing page on 2026-08-29. */}
                    <select class="cursor-api-model w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                      <option value="opus-5" data-provider="claude" data-input="5.0" data-output="25.0">Claude Opus 5</option>
                      <option value="sonnet-5" data-provider="claude" data-input="2.0" data-output="10.0">Claude Sonnet 5</option>
                      <option value="fable-5" data-provider="claude" data-input="10.0" data-output="50.0">Claude Fable 5</option>
                      <option value="opus-4-8" data-provider="claude" data-input="5.0" data-output="25.0">Claude Opus 4.8</option>
                      <option value="opus-4-7" data-provider="claude" data-input="5.0" data-output="25.0">Claude Opus 4.7</option>
                      <option value="sonnet-4-6" data-provider="claude" data-input="3.0" data-output="15.0">Claude Sonnet 4.6</option>
                      <option value="haiku-4-5" data-provider="claude" data-input="1.0" data-output="5.0">Claude Haiku 4.5</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-6-sol" data-provider="openai" data-input="4.0" data-output="20.0" class="hidden">GPT-5.6 Sol</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-6-terra" data-provider="openai" data-input="2.0" data-output="12.0" class="hidden">GPT-5.6 Terra</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-6-luna" data-provider="openai" data-input="0.2" data-output="1.2" class="hidden">GPT-5.6 Luna</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-5" data-provider="openai" data-input="5.0" data-output="30.0" class="hidden">GPT-5.5</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-4" data-provider="openai" data-input="2.5" data-output="15.0" class="hidden">GPT-5.4</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-4-mini" data-provider="openai" data-input="0.75" data-output="4.5" class="hidden">GPT-5.4 mini</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5" data-provider="openai" data-input="1.25" data-output="10.0" class="hidden">GPT-5</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-mini" data-provider="openai" data-input="0.25" data-output="2.0" class="hidden">GPT-5 mini</option>
                      <option value="gpt-5-nano" data-provider="openai" data-input="0.05" data-output="0.4" class="hidden">GPT-5 nano</option>
                      <option value="gpt-4o" data-provider="openai" data-input="2.5" data-output="10.0" class="hidden">GPT-4o</option>
                      <option value="o3" data-provider="openai" data-input="2.0" data-output="8.0" class="hidden">o3</option>
                      <option value="o3-mini" data-provider="openai" data-input="1.1" data-output="4.4" class="hidden">o3-mini</option>
                      <option value="gemini-3-1-pro" data-provider="gemini" data-input="2.0" data-output="12.0" class="hidden">Gemini 3.1 Pro (≤200k)</option>
                      <option value="gemini-3-7-flash" data-provider="gemini" data-input="0.75" data-output="3.75" class="hidden">Gemini 3.7 Flash</option>
                      <option value="gemini-3-5-flash" data-provider="gemini" data-input="1.5" data-output="9.0" class="hidden">Gemini 3.5 Flash</option>
                      <option value="gemini-3-5-flash-lite" data-provider="gemini" data-input="0.3" data-output="2.5" class="hidden">Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite</option>
                      <option value="gemini-2-5-pro" data-provider="gemini" data-input="1.25" data-output="10.0" class="hidden">Gemini 2.5 Pro (≤200k)</option>
                      <option value="gemini-2-5-flash" data-provider="gemini" data-input="0.3" data-output="2.5" class="hidden">Gemini 2.5 Flash</option>
                      <option value="gemini-2-5-flash-lite" data-provider="gemini" data-input="0.1" data-output="0.4" class="hidden">Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite</option>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Monthly Input Tokens</label>
                    <input type="number" min="0" value="500000" class="cursor-input-tokens w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <label class="block text-xs font-medium text-bae-muted mb-1.5">Monthly Output Tokens</label>
                    <input type="number" min="0" value="250000" class="cursor-output-tokens w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Reset -->
          <div class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-1">
